95f981917:docs/architecture/adr/ADR-0053-p6-operations-service-identities-exceptions-logs-heartbeat.md:79:- **The worker's freshness scan uses the same rule (amended 2026-11-04, T-DG6-ARCH-14; F-DG6-160; shipped by T-DG6-BE-Y3, F-DG6-100/F-DG6-140).** The scan's read (`apps/worker/src/handlers/operations.ts` `kpiFreshness`, the `data_stale` raiser in the table above) is the twin of `linkedKpiStatus`: the newest open or closed `reporting_period` of the organization and the KPI's frequency whose transformation-scope `period` evaluation (the slot's highest `calculation_run.seq`) has a non-null value, with the read-time staleness rule (`withReadTimeStaleness`, the active version's `dq_stale_after_days`). An empty or Unknown later period (for example the current month, opened by `kpi.reporting_period_open` and never filled by the stopped feed) therefore does **not** hide a stale value: the scan sees `stale`, emits one `data.stale` event per stale episode (idempotency key `data.stale:<kpiId>:<dataAsOf>`), and `operations.exception_raise` opens or recurs the KPI's `data_stale` exception (M0239). A KPI with no value in any period stays `unknown` with a null value and opens nothing; when the KPI is `fresh` again, the scan resolves the exception `recovered`. Tests: `apps/worker/test/integration/operations-freshness.test.ts` (the reviewer's scenario, an Unknown later evaluation, a Fresh control, a never-a-value control) and the parity test `apps/api/test/integration/operations/exception-last-known-value.test.ts` (the scan and `getOperationalException` agree). This replaces the earlier bullet "Not changed by this repair (open …)", which said the scan read only the newest period and left the rule undecided (see the amendment at the end of this ADR).
